WEBVTT

00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:19,740
CBC came back yesterday, everything fell into the normal range except my fasting glucose was 205 and my hemoglobin A1c was 6.0.

00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:24,740
This falls into the pre-diabetic range, correct?

00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:29,740
No, that actually falls into the full diabetic range.

00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:39,740
So if you had a 12 hour fast and your glucose is 205, that's not a good thing.

00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:42,740
So we got to start investigating this.

00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:50,740
I would like to look at, we should have a conversation to schedule an appointment.

00:00:50,740 --> 00:01:06,740
Technically, legally, glucose over a 12 hour fasting glucose over 125 for more than two consecutive blood tests is considered diabetes.

00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:16,740
So then when they came out with the hemoglobin A1c test, that's more of a specific test for long term glucose.

00:01:16,740 --> 00:01:27,740
We want to see that really below 5.5, at least, and yours being 6 is still elevated.

00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:36,740
So why concern what would be causing that elevated fasting glucose? So typically, you don't see an elevated fasting glucose.

00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:48,740
If you're fasting glucose of 205 unless the person has diabetes or something else going on, can be an error in the test.

00:01:48,740 --> 00:02:02,740
If all your other CBCs were all within normal limits and nothing was changed or your diet wasn't changed, nothing happened, and now you're at this spike, I mean, I would run it again.

00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:19,740
It's real easy to go get a glucometer at the target or a Walmart or something with the little prick, pin prick things and test your own fasting glucose to see if this is an abnormality or something was wrong with the lab.

00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,740
But that's abnormal.

00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:28,740
And the follow-up question I'm currently doing two green juices a day. I want to add apple and carrot, but wonder if it's too sweet.

00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:39,740
I should stay away from it. I would say with the fasting glucose of 205, I would not be adding apple and carrot juice right now. We got to figure this out something going on there.

00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:42,740
Hopefully it's just a lab error.

